  "id": "fatigue-studies",
  "term": "fatigue studies",
  "definition": "Fatigue studies are research investigations of mental fatigue, especially how prolonged demanding tasks affect tiredness, effort, attention, and performance over time. In this context, they often examine whether motivation, including intrinsic or extrinsic motivation, can lessen performance declines linked to mental fatigue.",
